cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and also cite
  Morgens et al. (2016), listed under references.
title: "castle-py3: casTLE for Python 3"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Jimmy
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3549-524X"
  - family-names: Morgens
    given-names: David W.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jimmykim014/castle-py3"
license: BSD-2-Clause
abstract: >-
  castle-py3 is a Python 3 port of casTLE (Cas9 high-Throughput maximum
  Likelihood Estimator) version 1.0, by David W Morgens, for analyzing
  pooled CRISPR and shRNA screens. It gives the same results as the
  original Python 2 scripts; the only change to output files is that
  genes are listed from highest to lowest casTLE score.
keywords:
  - CRISPR
  - RNAi
  - shRNA
  - genetic screens
  - casTLE
  - maximum likelihood
  - bioinformatics
  - Python 3
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Systematic comparison of CRISPR/Cas9 and RNAi screens for essential genes"
    authors:
      - family-names: Morgens
        given-names: David W.
      - family-names: Deans
        given-names: Richard M.
      - family-names: Li
        given-names: Amy
      - family-names: Bassik
        given-names: Michael C.
    journal: Nature Biotechnology
    year: 2016
    volume: 34
    start: 634
    end: 636
    doi: 10.1038/nbt.3567
  - type: software
    title: casTLE
    authors:
      - family-names: Morgens
        given-names: David W.
    version: "1.0"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/elifesciences-publications/dmorgens-castle"
